{
  "Name": "Klog Server authenticate.php user Unauthenticated Command Injection",
  "Description": "This module exploits an unauthenticated command injection vulnerability in Klog Server versions 2.4.1 and prior. The `authenticate.php` file uses the `user` HTTP POST parameter in a call to the `shell_exec()` PHP function without appropriate input validation, allowing arbitrary command execution as the apache user. The sudo configuration permits the apache user to execute any command as root without providing a password, resulting in privileged command execution as root. This module has been successfully tested on Klog Server version 2.4.1 virtual appliance.",
